# commands.words - Dingus Quest Zero's words, for what a command means to the game: the parser (games/dq0c, dq0c.s)
# fills the game's struct pcmd (dq0.h) by them, from the words of a line the grammar (commands.ebnf) has taken, and
# sim/tools/commandwords.js does the same on the host (the tests' reference).  They began as the old parser's tables
# (games/dq0/parse.c, 2026-10-19), word for word; what changed is marked "(new)".
#
# A section a kind of word; a line a word (or words, for a verb that is several) = its meaning, the names dq0.h,
# hub.h and level.h give (V_*, OR_*, H_*, OB_*, PR_*, HOW_*, SK_*).  A word is looked for as it was typed, then as
# the root its alias gives (commands.aliases), so an alias the player makes means what its root means.
#   [verbs]    the verb, if the line begins with it (several words first: "look closely" is examining)
#   [orders]   a request to an ally (V_TELL's order: the first)
#   [dirs]     a way: by the compass (H_*), as the character faces (REL n: an eighth turn n), GO_UP, GO_DOWN; two
#              together are the way between them
#   [things]   a kind of thing it can see (OB_*); PART: a part of one, its own word the thing's word too
#   [preps]    after the first thing, the other's: in it, on it, from it
#   [how]      up to it (HOW_TO) or through it (HOW_THROUGH)
#   [special]  words the meaning turns on: WITH (the other thing, used: whatever came before), WAY_OUT (the way out),
#              AWAY (put away: stowed), BACK (put back: not a way), HALF (a half turn), AROUND (turned or looked
#              round), BAR (put the bar ...: barred)
#   [styles]   a blow's verb, and what it strikes with (SK_*: the best to hand, unless one of these)
#   [little]   passed over

